WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.099 --> 00:00:04.660
You're not the boss of me.

00:00:04.660 --> 00:00:07.840
There's an enormous amount of rhetoric out
there about how strong the parties are, how

00:00:07.840 --> 00:00:10.650
terrible partisanship is.

00:00:10.650 --> 00:00:15.340
In both parties Bernie Sanders and Donald
Trump are supposedly incredibly brave for

00:00:15.340 --> 00:00:18.420
taking on the political establishment and
the political parties.

00:00:18.420 --> 00:00:23.000
And the simple reality is, if these parties
were so strong and powerful, neither of these

00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:25.160
guys would be able to do it.

00:00:25.160 --> 00:00:30.980
One of the dirtiest little secrets in Washington
for the last 30, 40 years has been the steady

00:00:30.980 --> 00:00:33.579
erosion of the strength of both political
parties.

00:00:33.579 --> 00:00:38.090
The era of the smoke filled room where party
elders picked a candidate was done away with

00:00:38.090 --> 00:00:39.659
by the primary system.

00:00:39.659 --> 00:00:43.800
Reforms in Congress have taken away the political
leverage and power that committee chairmen

00:00:43.800 --> 00:00:48.670
and party leadership used to have, and sort
of on every level if you're a celebrity, if

00:00:48.670 --> 00:00:53.440
you can get lots of people to vote for you,
that's the only power you need.

00:00:53.440 --> 00:00:57.600
One thing that Donald Trump recognized is
that in a democracy, particularly in the modern

00:00:57.600 --> 00:01:00.690
media age, being a celebrity is incredible
power.

00:01:00.690 --> 00:01:05.610
And if you get people to show up to vote for
you, that's all the power you need to overrule

00:01:05.610 --> 00:01:08.170
the political parties.

00:01:08.170 --> 00:01:11.370
So what do you think about the weakness or
strength of the political parties?

00:01:11.370 --> 00:01:14.840
Let us know in the comments, and also let
us know what other topics you might like to

00:01:14.840 --> 00:01:16.310
see us cover in 60 seconds.

